# Extension Principle

Handbooks extend constitutional principles.

They do not redefine them.

Examples:

Architecture explains architectural responsibilities.

Database explains persistent data.

Security explains protection strategies.

The Constitution defines the underlying philosophy.

Avoid repeating constitutional content.

---

# Knowledge Boundaries

Each handbook should remain focused.

Avoid introducing:

Database standards inside Frontend.

UI standards inside Database.

Infrastructure standards inside Product.

Business workflow definitions inside Tailwind.

Knowledge boundaries improve clarity.

---

# Cross-Handbook References

When concepts span multiple domains:

Reference.

Do not duplicate.

Example:

Security references Database ownership.

Database references Architecture ownership.

Architecture references Constitutional principles.

Cross-referencing preserves consistency.

